  "tagline": "The open-source core of GemFire: a consistent, partitioned in-memory data grid for Java.",
  "description": "Apache Geode is the open-sourced core of GemFire, donated by Pivotal in 2015. It provides partitioned and replicated regions with strong consistency, OQL queries, continuous queries, function execution and WAN gateways between clusters. After development stalled and the PMC voted in 2024 to retire it, a group of contributors revived the project, shipping 1.15.2 in 2025 and a modernised 2.0 (Java 17, Jakarta EE 10) announced in January 2026, with 2.0.3 in September 2026. It is again usable, but most enterprise users get the same technology through Tanzu GemFire.",
